hat allows you to quickly deploy MID Servers at scale.Containerized MID Server uses a Docker image of the MID Server that allows you to quickly deploy MID Servers at scale. MID Servers are deployed using orchestration tools like Docker Swarm.You can configure containerized MID Servers with configuration parameters passed through environment variables or secret files.You can configure containerized MID Servers with configuration parameters passed through environment variables or secret files.You can configure containerized MID Servers with configuration parameters passed through environment variables or secret files.You can configure containerized MID Servers with configuration parameters passed through environment variables or secret files.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/mid-server/mid-build-docker-linux.html","release":"australia","product":"MID Server","classification":"mid-server","topic_type":"task","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":14,"breadcrumb":["Containerized MID Server","Configuring MID Servers","Configuring MID Server","MID Server","Manage instance data sources","Extend ServiceNow AI Platform capabilities"],"tags":["#servicenow-platform","#mid-server","#on-premise","#proxy","#connectivity","#type-task"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[115,117],[121,126],[130,134],[307,346],[382,421]],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/servicenow-platform/mid-server/mid-build-docker-linux.md"},
